tool-mode-corpus.json.fresh
.tools/

# @vscode/test-electron download cache (R3/M25 e2e artifacts)
.vscode-test/

# M55.V1 rig's isolated VS Code profile: a LOCAL 74 MB install artifact (the
# fresh-VSIX install under test). The frames and the session manifest are the
# evidence and ARE committed; this profile is machine-local and never is.
validation/m55/profile/

# client-tooling client runtime dir
.client-tooling/

# tree-sitter grammar build outputs. `tree-sitter generate` writes a ~16MB
# parser.c and the node-types/grammar JSON, and `tree-sitter build` writes a
# local wasm; only the hand-written grammar sources (grammar.js, package.json,
# tree-sitter.json, README, scanner.h) are tracked. The wasm the product loads
# is the one committed under wasm/, which is the artifact the evidence names.
# NOTE: the pattern excludes the CONTENTS of src/, not the directory, because
# git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded -- the
# scanner.c negation below is inert if this reads `src/`.
grammars/tree-sitter-*/src/*
grammars/tree-sitter-*/tree-sitter-*.wasm
# ...EXCEPT hand-written external scanners, which are SOURCE, not build output.
# The set of grammar source files that must be tracked for a rebuild is named in
# the comment above as "grammar.js, package.json, tree-sitter.json, README,
# scanner.h" -- and `scanner.h` covers the headers an in-tree scanner dir holds.
# tree-sitter-cpp's external scanner is `src/scanner.c`, so the blanket `src/`
# ignore silently dropped the one file its grammar cannot be rebuilt without.
# Found while vendoring tree-sitter-cpp for #743: the ignore list named the
# scanner by its C++-in-fsharp-style filename instead of by its role.
!grammars/tree-sitter-cpp/src/scanner.c

# tree-sitter-perl (1.2.1, vendored by the M14.6 perl wave) needs the same three
# roles, plus one more this grammar has: its external scanner at `src/scanner.c`
# includes `tree_sitter/parser.h`, so the header tree is SOURCE here and not
# build output — without it the vendored scanner cannot be compiled and the lane
# has no rebuild path. `src/parser.c` (29 MB, regenerated by
# `tree-sitter generate`) stays ignored, and so do the per-language generated
# scanner headers `tsp_*.h`/`bsearch.h`, which `tree-sitter generate` copies in
# alongside parser.c.
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/grammar.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/scanner.c
# ...and the header DIRECTORY has to be un-ignored before the files inside it
# can be: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded (the
# same trap the note above records for `src/`), so the negation is two levels.
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/tree_sitter/
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/tree_sitter/parser.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/tree_sitter/alloc.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-perl/src/tree_sitter/array.h
# tree-sitter-vbnet (govindbanura/tree-sitter-vbnet, vendored AND heavily
# PATCHED by the M60 VB wave -- 18 repairs, each with a repro case under
# fixtures/grammar-repro/cases) needs the same two generated files as nim and
# hcl, for the same reason: they are what `script/m14/verify-grammar-pins.ts`
# reads to run its offline source<->wasm proof. Without them the pin's check
# reports "not applicable" and the lane has no proof that the committed wasm is a
# build of the committed grammar -- which for a patched grammar is the one claim
# that matters most, since the patches live in `grammar.js`.
# `src/parser.c` (29 MB, regenerated by `tree-sitter generate`) stays ignored,
# the same call made for perl: unlike graphql's 283 KB, 29 MB is not something to
# put in git for hermeticity. The rebuild path is
# `tree-sitter generate && tree-sitter build --wasm`, and the two JSON files are
# the digest-stable evidence that a regeneration changed nothing that matters.
!grammars/tree-sitter-vbnet/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-vbnet/src/grammar.json
# tree-sitter-xml (tree-sitter-grammars 0.7.0 @ 5000ae8f, vendored AND PATCHED
# by the M60 xml lane) needs the same roles graphql took, plus ONE this grammar
# uniquely has: its external scanner is a HEADER, `common/scanner.h`, shared by
# both the `xml` and `dtd` grammars and included by `xml/src/scanner.c`. That
# makes `common/scanner.h` SOURCE, not build output — and it is the file the M60
# repair edits (`skip_if_eq` in `scan_pi_content`), so if it went untracked the
# repair would be invisible in the diff and unrebuildable from the repository.
# The layout is upstream's (`<lang>/` per grammar, `common/` shared), so the
# patterns are nested one level deeper than the flat grammars.
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/common/scanner.h
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/common/common.mjs
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/xml/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/xml/src/grammar.json
# ...and `xml/src/parser.c` too: 254 KB, the same call hcl (600 KB) and graphql
# (283 KB) made. With it tracked, the wired wasm is rebuildable from TRACKED files
# alone, so `measureVendored`'s per-file digests do not move on a `tree-sitter
# generate` that changed nothing else.
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/xml/src/parser.c
# ...and `xml/src/scanner.c`, which `#include`s the shared header above and is
# therefore equally required for a rebuild.
!grammars/tree-sitter-xml/xml/src/scanner.c
# tree-sitter-hcl (tree-sitter-grammars 1.2.0 @ 64ad6278, vendored for the M60
# HCL lane): the grammar-pin instrument's offline source↔wasm proof needs the
# two GENERATED files (`script/m14/verify-grammar-pins.ts` `sourceVsWasmFor`),
# and without them the pin would record a sha with no proof that the wired bytes
# are a build of the committed source — which is the whole property the pin buys
# over an unversioned blob.
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/node-types.json
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/grammar.json
# ...and the two files the wasm is REBUILT from. Unlike haskell (20 MB) and
# elixir (13 MB) this parser is 600 KB, so it is kept: the pin then rebuilds
# offline rather than resting on a hash alone.
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/parser.c
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/scanner.c
# ...and the tree-sitter headers `parser.c` includes, without which a rebuild
# fails at the preprocessor rather than at the grammar.
!grammars/tree-sitter-hcl/src/tree_sitter/
